          "severity": "P2",
          "title": "A blocked job with an active status shows two icons stacked in the same corner",
          "body": "The blocked icon and the new state icon both use `position: absolute; top: 5px; right: 6px`, so they draw on top of each other. The PR says the markers sit \"next to the existing blocked icon\", and that is not true when both apply. `jobNode` sets `blocked` when there is any open blocker (`web/src/App.tsx:2797`), and a blocker does not change the job's status. `src/mcp.ts:454` records a blocker without a status change, and `no_convergence` is raised from the review path (`src/reviews.ts:114`). So a job in `in_progress`, `in_review` or `delivering` with an open blocker renders the blocked circle and the blue arc or green eye in the same 14px box. The pulse of the blocked icon also runs over the new icon. Fix: move the state icon to a second slot (for example `right: 26px`) when `n.blocked` is set, or drop the state icon while blocked, and state the choice in the PR and the guide.",
